00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:53.440
It appears to be targetting objects with flowing
electricity, such as the transformers of utility poles.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.650
Power outages have been reported in various places—

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.320
The radio waves might be the only thing drawing them in.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.320
What do we do?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.700
I doubt the Gyro will do any good in this situation...

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.700
Hey!

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.410
Quit screwin' around! Let's hit the road!

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.910
Go...? Where to?

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:11.420
We'll use the Gyro you guys modified 
to draw those bastards outta town!

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.410
Hop to it and get yer ass ready!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.340
Let's give it our best shot.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.450
First stop is the station front.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.930
There it is!

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.810
Well, ain't that perfect!

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.730
They can be our test subjects!

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.810
Well Sacchan, you better lock up!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.570
Bye now. Take care out there.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.780
Archetype?

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:45.660
It's a generic name for the weirdly-shaped 
molecule that Professor Li is researching.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.240
This is an Archetype?

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.370
It hasn't been successfully synthesized yet, has it?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.830
We have to go back home.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.170
Please make an exception. 
Could you stop at the next station?

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.250
What's going on?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.260
I believe this is the cause.

