00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.460
What if we use the car's transceiver?

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.880
They react to electromagnetic radiation.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.050
Using the transmitter isn't a good idea.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.330
This isn't good!

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.190
Hello. Do you copy?

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.480
This is Tachibana from the No. 6 bus.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.310
Do you copy?

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:08.960
We are currently under attack by 
the Rodan and require immediate aid.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.490
Finally come to say hello, huh.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.910
I'll distract them with my bow.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.150
A bow?

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:24.420
I'm a 5-dan in archery.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:24.830
Leave it to m—

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:30.920
We've done it now!

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.090
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:35.220
What's the plan? Do we take a risk 
and charge towards the bus?

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.590
Is that yours?

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:38.590
Yeah.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.640
Could you lend it to me? 
I'll need those plastic bottles, too.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.100
Yung. Please calculate.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.350
Proceed.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.810
What's the highest frequency component 
of the Rodan's screeches?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.980
It is around 800 hertz.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.370
That's one octave higher than our reference tones...

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:55.110
What if we convert it to wavelengths?

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.990
The sound wave would be around 40cm.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:03.630
Both sides are closed ends, 
and halving the wavelength leaves us with 20cm.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.830
It's likely to work.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.580
Any software to perform a wind tunnel calculation?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:12.170
We are limited to very simple functions 
with limited internet access.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.840
Please simulate this one for me.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:18.050
Scanning. Please continue rotating it gently.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.550
Scan complete.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.910
Begin tracing.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.230
Tracing complete. We can begin the simulation.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:29.480
Test a few samples.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.400
Please define the speed.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.110
60 meters per second.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.230
Simulation complete. Please specify a—

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.620
Alright! Give me the location of the hole, 
its diameter, and its number.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:44.680
A hole?

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.470
Roger. Producing the blueprint.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.630
That smoke! It was near my apartment...

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.170
This is bad news for your laundry...

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.890
Forget that. Show me how the town's doing.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.180
Roger! Let us hurry!

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.030
This isn't good.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:17.990
We're done.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:19.360
Shoot these for me.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:20.900
Okay.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:23.840
Damn it...

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.700
I beesech your aid, O Great God of Arms!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.720
Try pulling it a little harder.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.120
You will produce more effective noise.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.000
That is perfect.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:52.730
Okay!

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:00.560
Now!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.180
Let's go!

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.390
A whistling arrow to commence battle, eh?

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.410
Oh, hell!

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.970
Hold your horses!

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.130
I won!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.830
Ka-ching! That'll teach you!

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.630
Wait, hold up! Damn you!

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.250
Huh? Wait—

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.730
What happened?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.230
At that speed, they probably managed to escape.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.980
This train will temporarily stop at the next station.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.240
We apologize for the inconvenience caused.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:36.080
Not much longer until our battery dries up.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:49.850
Just like before...

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.820
This is the state of Nigashio at dawn.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.070
A considerable amount of 
damage can be seen across the area.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.820
The scattered blue sheets you see 
are covering Rodan carcasses.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:56.830
There are 13 confirmed missing people cases, 
while 143 others have been hospitalized.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:58.830
Maybe it failed to dissipate its heat?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.830
When creatures that don't sweat overexert themselves...

